{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And the Avvim, who dwelt in Chatzerim as far as Gaza.</b> Now it explains where the Chavvim were. And the Avvim is like the Chavvim — the ayin and the chet interchange. And the Chavvim — if you wish to know where they are: in Chatzerim they dwell, for they were not concerned to dwell in walled cities, because they were mighty. And 'the land of the Rephaim' is the kingdom of Og, as it is written: 'that was called the land of Rephaim.' 'It is what I gave to Avraham their father' — they came and possessed it. But the land of Moav, which they took from the Emim, who are as great as the Anakim — the Rephaim there is not the same Rephaim that 'I gave to Avraham,' for the Moavites call them, etc. And also the land of the children of Ammon, which they took from the Zamzummim — that too is not the same Rephaim, for the Ammonites call them Zamzummim, and they were not called Rephaim except because Rephaim had dwelt in it."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The phrase 'כי המואבים יקראו כו׳ is cut short by וגו׳; rendered as 'the Moavites call them, etc.' The scriptural quotation ההוא יקרא ארץ רפאים is from Deuteronomy 3:13; the following words appear to be the compiler's own continuation woven into the citation, translated as they stand."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:00:25.210455981Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}